# Normalise line endings so a Windows checkout cannot commit CRLF.
#
# There was no .gitattributes here, so what got stored depended on whoever
# committed and how their core.autocrlf happened to be set. Prettier is
# configured with endOfLine: "lf" and CI checks it, so a single CRLF file is a
# red build — and on a Windows working tree the failure is invisible locally,
# because the checkout has CRLF either way.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what is text; eol=lf pins what text is stored and
# checked out as. The explicit binary list below is not decoration: `text=auto`
# guesses, and a wrong guess on an image or a model file corrupts it silently
# by rewriting bytes that happen to look like line endings.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Images and icons
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary

# Audio and models
*.wav binary
*.onnx binary
*.gguf binary

# Fonts
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Archives and compiled artefacts
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.dll binary
*.dylib binary
*.so binary
*.lib binary
*.pdf binary

# SVG is text and benefits from normalisation, so it is deliberately not listed
# above — it is XML, and diffs of it are worth reading.
